---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/global/Header";
import Footer from "../components/global/Footer";

import "../styles/main.scss";
---

<Layout title="Delete Your Account · Bibliolab">
  <Header client:load />

  <main>
    <section class="delete-account | wrapper">
      <p class="delete-account__eyebrow">Account &amp; privacy</p>
      <h1 class="delete-account__title">Delete your Bibliolab account</h1>
      <p class="delete-account__intro">
        You can permanently delete your Bibliolab account and associated data
        directly in the app or by contacting our support team by email.
      </p>

      <div class="delete-account__notice">
        <strong>Before you continue:</strong>
        Account deletion is permanent. Your profile, reading activity, lists, and
        other account data may not be recoverable after the request is completed.
        Deleting your Bibliolab account does not automatically cancel a subscription
        purchased through Apple or Google; cancel that subscription through the store
        where you purchased it.
      </div>

      <h2>Option 1: Delete through the app</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Bibliolab and sign in to the account you want to delete.</li>
        <li>Open your profile or account settings.</li>
        <li>
          Select <strong>Delete account</strong> and follow the confirmation steps.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Option 2: Request deletion by email</h2>
      <p>
        Send your request to
        <a
          href="mailto:bibliolabsofficial@gmail.com?subject=Bibliolab%20account%20deletion%20request"
          >bibliolabsofficial@gmail.com</a
        >. Use the subject line <strong
          >Bibliolab account deletion request</strong
        >
        and include the following information:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>The email address associated with your Bibliolab account.</li>
        <li>Your Bibliolab display name or username, if you have one.</li>
        <li>How you sign in, such as email, Google, or Apple.</li>
        <li>
          Any non-sensitive account detail that helps us locate the account,
          such as your approximate sign-up date or the title of a saved book.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="delete-account__verification">
        <h3>How we verify ownership</h3>
        <p>
          The strongest and simplest proof of ownership is sending the request
          from the email address registered to your Bibliolab account. We may
          reply to that address to confirm the request before deleting anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you no longer have access to that email address, tell us in your
          request. We may ask for additional non-sensitive information that
          matches the account before we can proceed. For your protection, never
          send us your password, one-time codes, recovery codes, or complete
          payment-card details.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <p>
        We will review the request, contact you if ownership confirmation is
        needed, and confirm by email when the deletion has been completed. If
        you only want to stop emails or cancel a subscription, mention that in
        your message instead of requesting account deletion.
      </p>

      <p class="delete-account__contact">
        Questions? Contact
        <a href="mailto:bibliolabsofficial@gmail.com"
          >bibliolabsofficial@gmail.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
